# Title: Potential Persistence Via App Paths Default Property
# ID: 707e097c-e20f-4f67-8807-1f72ff4500d6
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-10
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.t1546.012
# Description: Detects changes to the "Default" property for keys located in the \Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\ registry. Which might be used as a method of persistence
# The entries found under App Paths are used primarily for the following purposes.
# First, to map an application's executable file name to that file's fully qualified path.
# Second, to prepend information to the PATH environment variable on a per-application, per-process basis.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(registry.path:*\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths* AND (registry.path:*(Default) OR registry.path:*Path) AND (registry.data.strings:*\\Users\\Public* OR registry.data.strings:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\* OR registry.data.strings:*\\Windows\\Temp\\* OR registry.data.strings:*\\Desktop\\* OR registry.data.strings:*\\Downloads\\* OR registry.data.strings:*%temp%* OR registry.data.strings:*%tmp%* OR registry.data.strings:*iex* OR registry.data.strings:*Invoke-* OR registry.data.strings:*rundll32* OR registry.data.strings:*regsvr32* OR registry.data.strings:*mshta* OR registry.data.strings:*cscript* OR registry.data.strings:*wscript* OR registry.data.strings:*.bat* OR registry.data.strings:*.hta* OR registry.data.strings:*.dll* OR registry.data.strings:*.ps1*))
